From 6513fce9fc0cb2a4b96899325de960efaa4872ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:02:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vulkan): bounded host split with explicit staging
 reserve (R46b B7c)

Carve a staging reserve out of the host-visible heap before any bulk
admission, then let the loader transaction place a bounded, deterministic
subset of weight buffers on host memory instead of refusing; unbounded host
placement stays impossible. Switches GGML_VK_STAGING_RESERVE and
GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MAX documented in OPTIONS-REGISTRY. Independent review
PASS. HQ load cells: 27B Q4_K_XL fits with no split; 27B S-X8 admits a
bounded split and is refused with GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MAX=0; 84 GB refused
before any allocation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp,ggml-vulkan-types.h,ggml-vulkan.cpp; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_593.py)
